FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/repl/bytecode_view.rs:55 — `compile()` calls `compile_source` (which runs `analyze` with an empty scope per src/bytecode/format.rs:278) so `.bytecode say x` reports unknown-variable for a session-bound `x` while `say x` runs via `analyze_with_bound_names` (src/repl/mod.rs:1140, src/repl/mod.rs:1935) — why it matters: the listing answers about a different program than the session would run, contradicting the "same frontend" claim — concrete fix: thread session names into the bytecode-view compile path or refuse by name when unbound names are present.
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2007 — `print_code_answer` prints every line of `render_compact` (src/bytecode/disasm.rs:35) with no output cap, bypassing `MAX_BLOCK_LINES`/`MAX_BLOCK_BYTES` because `handle_command` runs before `execute_line` buffering — why it matters: unbounded resource use reachable from one pasted `.bytecode` line, admitted in FINDINGS.md — concrete fix: cap printed lines with a truncation notice pointing at `rb dis` for the rest.
3. [MAJOR] src/repl/bytecode_view.rs:220 — `edge_nothing_to_compile_is_a_refusal_and_not_an_empty_listing` tests only `bytecode_lines("   ")`, never `asm_lines("   ")`, while the refusal differs by command name (src/repl/bytecode_view.rs:50) — why it matters: the `asm` empty path is an untested new branch, and the weak check at src/repl/bytecode_view.rs:199 (`contains("Error") || contains("error")`) pins no parser error/caret — concrete fix: assert both commands refuse empty input by name with no listing.
4. [MINOR] src/bytecode/disasm.rs:62 — `render_compact_blocks` destructures `blank_before: _` and never emits the separator blank line that `render_blocks` emits at src/bytecode/disasm.rs:144, leaving dead `blank_before:true` at src/bytecode/disasm.rs:54 and src/bytecode/disasm.rs:79 — why it matters: REPORT claims the only difference is constants-table plus comments, but blank-line separation also differs and is unpinned — concrete fix: drop the dead field from the compact walk or emit the same separators and correct the docs.
5. [MINOR] tests/repl_test.rs:1221 — `bytecode_reports_a_compile_error_instead_of_listing_nothing` drives `.bytecode` and `:asm` in one session and only checks combined stdout contains `Error` and lacks `redblue bytecode` — why it matters: one command reporting plus the other crashing still passes, and no parser error/caret is pinned unlike the unit test — concrete fix: isolate per-command output and assert each reports the frontend error with no listing.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
